{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"CE PERSONA-LOSS RATE, computed per ATTEMPT rather than per surviving artifact - the clearest demonstration of the denominator problem in this census. Four of the eleven Wave 3 CE runs (36 percent) required at least one retry because a persona was lost; across roughly fifteen attempts that is about 27 percent of attempts. THE SCORED ARTIFACTS ALONE WOULD REPORT ZERO PERCENT, because every loss was retried until it succeeded and the retry overwrote the failure. The rate is recoverable only because degraded attempts were preserved in superseded/ and runs/replicates/ rather than deleted. Breakdown: go-gitea, the calibration control, lost coherence and design-lens on attempt one and reached 7 of 7 on retry; kotlin-thunderbird lost three personas and reached 7 of 7 on retry; scss-uswds lost coherence on attempt one and reached 7 of 7 on attempt two, which also produced 43 findings against attempt one's 33; ts-carbon returned a full team on attempt one, lost coherence on attempt two, and a third attempt is running. Preserving failed attempts is therefore not archival tidiness - it is the only thing that makes tool reliability measurable."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789444401188307001,"uuid":"7d97a313-105d-496a-ac2c-1bdd8c741b14"}